problem:
In triangle $ABC$, $AB = 3$, $AC = 5$, and $BC = 4$.  The medians $AD$, $BE$, and $CF$ of triangle $ABC$ intersect at the centroid $G$.  Let the projections of $G$ onto $BC$, $AC$, and $AB$ be $P$, $Q$, and $R$, respectively.  Find $GP + GQ + GR$.

[asy]
import geometry;

unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, P, Q, R;

A = (0,3);
B = (0,0);
C = (4,0);
D = (B + C)/2;
E = (C + A)/2;
F = (A + B)/2;
G = (A + B + C)/3;
P = (G + reflect(B,C)*(G))/2;
Q = (G + reflect(C,A)*(G))/2;
R = (G + reflect(A,B)*(G))/2;

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--G);
draw(B--G);
draw(C--G);
draw(G--P);
draw(G--Q);
draw(G--R);

label("$A$", A, dir(90));
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$G$", G, SE);
label("$P$", P, S);
label("$Q$", Q, NE);
label("$R$", R, W);
[/asy]The answer is in the form \frac{m}{n}, where gcd(m, n) = 1. Please provide the value of m + n.

